lumina-lock (0.4.30) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The power menu works on every screen. It used to open a single window on
    whichever screen happened to be active; now every screen gets one, so the
    whole desktop dims rather than one monitor, and the controls are drawn only
    on the screen the pointer is on. That is the same rule the password field
    follows, and for the same reason: the pointer is the only hint of which
    screen someone is looking at.
  * Crossing between screens carries the controls across. The screen they leave
    runs them off toward the other one on an accelerating curve, and that one
    brings them in from the same side on a decelerating one, a beat later. Two
    halves, one movement — moving both at once reads as two copies of the panel
    rather than one being carried.
  * The dim is a single value every window reads, so pulling the slide darkens
    all of them. On a single screen, where the value still has to travel through
    the same path: (3,5,9) at rest, (0,0,0) with the knob all the way over.
  * The keyboard grab follows the controls, the way it follows the password
    field.
  * Not yet exercised: the multi-screen path itself. Qt identifies screens
    through XRandR outputs and the test environment has one, so it reports
    windows=1 there and the handoff could not be triggered — the per-screen
    window creation and the handoff animation are unproven. Worth checking on a
    real pair: the menu dims both screens, the controls sit on the pointer's
    screen, and dragging the pointer across carries them over in two beats.

