lumina-lock (0.4.23) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fixed Escape doing nothing to the power menu when it was opened from the
    lock screen. Key routing happens in ScreenManager::eventFilter, which runs
    before the focused item sees anything: with no screen picked for
    authentication yet — the idle lock — the screen under the pointer is never
    the auth screen, so every keystroke was consumed as "wake this screen up".
    Escape went to the lock and the menu had no keyboard way out. The filter now
    stands aside while the power menu is up, because the menu holds the grab and
    its own item has the focus.
  * The lock screen's session controls belong to the password screen rather than
    to the idle lock, and they arrive with a tail: a 55 ms offset between the two
    so they read as one gesture with something trailing, and an OutBack curve so
    they rise past where they belong and settle back into it. Frames from a
    screen recording show the second button still low while the first is up, and
    both aligned once settled.
  * Hovering one of them is visible now: the fill goes to 26% white, the rim to
    the focus value, and the disc grows by 8%. An invisible control that still
    takes clicks would be worse than no control, so they are only there when the
    password field is.

