lumina-lock (0.4.10-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fixed the lock screen flashing its content on every re-lock: the clock
    appeared at full opacity, faded out, then faded back in. The surfaces stay
    alive between locks, so when a re-lock resets the scene the clock was
    still at the opacity the previous lock left it at. resetForLock() clears
    `animating` precisely so the layout snaps back to Idle instead of
    animating, but the clock's entry reveal and the hint's reveal did not
    honour it: they animated the *hide* with the same 480 ms fade that is
    meant for the reveal, while the window was being shown at the same time.
    Both are now gated on `animating`, like the transition properties already
    were.
    Measured over a lock -> unlock -> lock cycle, the clock region used to run
    97 -> 95/89/87/89/93/96/97 (down, then back up) once the window reappeared;
    it now holds the wallpaper's own brightness and rises monotonically once.
  * The cold-start path never showed this: a plain launch starts already
    locked, so resetForLock() is never called. Only the resident daemon
    (`--daemon`, the mode the package installs) reaches it, on the second and
    every later lock.

