lumina-lock (0.4.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Lock-screen polish:
    - Frosted glass behind the clock/date and the password field: each panel
      samples only the wallpaper region it covers, blurs it and clips it to a
      rounded shape, so an idle lock screen does no per-frame blur work. Falls
      back to a translucent surface on video wallpapers and on software
      scene-graph backends.
    - Clock and date font weight are configurable (thin … bold) via DConfig
      and the control-center plugin.
    - Busy indicator is now an arc covering a fifth of the ring instead of a
      single travelling dot.
    - Unlock transition: the video decoder is frozen before the fade starts,
      content fades before the window, and the per-frame content scaling is
      gone — that scaling of the large clock type was the main source of
      stutter, worst right after the wallpaper had loaded.
    - The clock now fades in on a short beat after lock (and once the
      wallpaper can draw), instead of popping in over a half-decoded image.
  * Keyboard and pointer are grabbed while locked (X11), so window-manager
    shortcuts such as Alt+Tab can no longer switch away from the lock; the
    grab is released on unlock.
  * Package now depends on qml6-module-qtquick-effects and
    qml6-module-qtquick-shapes (and, since the previous build,
    qml6-module-qtquick-dialogs); the control-center plugin uses Qt Quick
    dialogs instead of QFileDialog, which aborted the control center because
    it runs on QGuiApplication.

